Vectors, coordinate fields and flux (@em-vectorfields: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Vector-Calculus-Tong.lingua#r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5", #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA", #electromagnetism "../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/models/Small-changes-and-derivatives.lingua#r_4T51QH8VRCNNMY5WD30VJS5P52") { r_65BCQQW5JWE20Y2P34YD6AD09V
**Read:** [Vector Calculus — David Tong](../sources/Vector-Calculus-Tong.lingua#r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5), curves, surfaces, coordinates and integral geometry; [Electromagnetics Volume 1 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-1-Ellingson.lingua#r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA), chapter 4 in full.

A field assigns a value to every point and time in its domain. Components depend on the coordinate basis; the physical vector does not change when axes rotate. Draw a uniform field and a point-charge field in Cartesian and spherical coordinates. A radial unit vector changes with position even when a radial field coefficient depends only on radius.

Use dot products to project field through a surface and cross products to express magnetic force. Fix a surface normal and loop orientation together by the right-hand rule. Reversing a chosen normal changes the sign of flux without changing the apparatus. A field-line drawing can show direction and qualitative density, but it is not a collection of physical strings or a unique representation of magnitude.

Calculate the flux of a constant E through a rectangle inclined by angle θ: Φ = EA cos θ. Then compare a closed cube in the same field, where outward contributions cancel. Work rotations, Jacobians and differential line/area/volume elements before replacing a geometric integral by a remembered coordinate formula. [Vector Calculus — David Tong](../sources/Vector-Calculus-Tong.lingua#r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5) supplies a complete mathematical course for this work.

**Continue:** [Small changes, derivatives, and first-order approximations](../../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/models/Small-changes-and-derivatives.lingua#r_4T51QH8VRCNNMY5WD30VJS5P52).

**Return:** [Electromagnetism — charge, fields, matter, waves and physical evidence](../Electromagnetism.lingua#r_5TJPESCTTNAKY66JH2QNQYN1PY).
